
  <sn><md>### Distribution and Transformation of Pollutants

Pollutants released into the environment do not remain at their original location. They **move between environmental compartments** and undergo various **physical, chemical, and biological transformations**. These two processes are called **distribution** and **transformation**.

**Distribution** is the `movement and partitioning` of pollutants among the **atmosphere, hydrosphere, geosphere, and biosphere**.

```text
                    POLLUTANT SOURCE
                          │
             ┌────────────┼────────────┐
             ↓            ↓            ↓
        Atmosphere    Hydrosphere   Geosphere
             │            │            │
             └────────────┼────────────┘
                          ↓
                      Biosphere
                          │
                  Food chain / organisms
```
</md></sn>
